1
00:05:56,666 --> 00:06:02,666
American Movie is a documentary, comedy film directed by Chris Smith.

2
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:59,333
American Movie documents the story of filmmaker Mark
Borchardt, his mission, and his dream.

3
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Spanning over two years of intense struggle with his film, his family, financial decline, and spiritual crisis,
American Movie is a portrayal of ambition, obsession, excess, and one man's quest for the American Dream.

4
00:23:46,666 --> 00:23:52,666
Filmmaker, played by Mark Borchardt.

5
00:29:43,333 --> 00:29:49,333
Friend / Musician, played by Mike Schank.

6
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Actor in 'Coven', played by Tom Schimmels.

7
00:41:36,666 --> 00:41:42,666
Mark's Mom, played by Monica Borchardt.

8
00:47:33,333 --> 00:47:39,333
Mark's Brother, played by Alex Borchardt.

9
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Mark's Brother, played by Chris Borchardt.

10
00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:32,666
American Movie is a 1999 American documentary film directed by Chris Smith, produced
by Smith and Sarah Price, and edited by Jun Diaz and Barry Poltermann.

11
01:05:23,333 --> 01:05:29,333
Filmed between September 1995 and August 1997, American Movie documents the making of
Coven, an independent short horror film directed by Mark Borchardt.

12
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Produced for the purpose of raising capital for Northwestern, a feature film Borchardt intends to make, Coven suffers from numerous setbacks, including
poor financing, a lack of planning, Borchardt's alcoholism, and the ineptitude of the friends and family he enlists as his production team.

13
01:17:16,666 --> 01:17:22,666
The documentary follows Borchardt's filmmaking process, interspersed
with footage from both of Borchardt's developing projects.

14
01:23:13,333 --> 01:23:19,333
American Movie received positive reviews and won the Grand Jury Prize
for Documentary at the 1999 Sundance Film Festival.

15
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:16,000
It has since become a cult film.

16
01:35:06,666 --> 01:35:12,666
The film explores themes of underdog, obsession, wisconsin, beer, ambition.

17
01:41:03,333 --> 01:41:09,333
The tone is lighthearted and intense.
